      "message": "I wonder if this isn\u0027t something that we should put in RpcHardwareInfo, with the VTS just enforcing a minimum bound of 10.\n\nSince TEE\u0027s are less memory sensitive, and also likely to be the bulk of provisioning requests, I\u0027d rather we avoid cases of doing a lot of extra round trips to provision TEE IRPC instances just to have a blanket accommodation for SE\u0027s.\n\nAdditionally, we may need to consider modifying the Trusty HAL service / TA implementation to chunk this HAL call into multiple requests once there is a real DICE chain being passed in from GSA, as this will add a lot of memory pressure and is easily decomposable from the top level CSR array.",
